<title>SINGAPORE: Surreyville holds 49.7 pct Tri-M shares.</title>
<headline>Surreyville holds 49.7 pct Tri-M shares.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Surreyville Pte Ltd said on Thursday it now held 14.9 million shares in electronics firm Tri-M Technologies (S) Ltd as of March 5 1997.</p>
<p>The shares represented 49.73 percent of Tri-M's issued share capital, HSBC Investment Bank Asia Ltd said in a statement on behalf of Surreyville.</p>
<p>Tri-M is subject to a multi-dollar takeover bid from Surreyville.</p>
<p>Surreyville had early agreed to buy the combined 14 million Tri-M shares or 46.6 percent from Mitsubishi Corp and Miyoshi Electronics Corp at US$1.10 each.  </p>
<p>It also made a cash offer of Singapore $0.80 for each of Tri-M remaining 16 million shares in January.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
